From 04adf81e2949e1a0574dc6859443a731ecad5faf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ElXreno <elxreno@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 03:40:07 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7925: arm the sniffer when a monitor vif gets
 its channel context

mt7925_assign_vif_chanctx() only records the context. The sniffer
commands are sent from mt7925_change_chanctx(), which runs when the
context changes, not when it is first assigned. An active monitor
that starts on its target channel therefore never enables the
sniffer and receives nothing.

Send UNI_SNIFFER enable and config on assignment for monitor vifs,
the same way mt7925_change_chanctx() does.

Link: https://github.com/morrownr/USB-WiFi/issues/682#issuecomment-4115109552
---
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7925/main.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7925/main.c b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7925/main.c
index 0b7666dddb3d..443018638ddd 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7925/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7925/main.c
@@ -2347,6 +2347,13 @@ static int mt7925_assign_vif_chanctx(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 	mctx->bss_conf = mconf;
 	mutex_unlock(&dev->mt76.mutex);
 
+	if (vif->type == NL80211_IFTYPE_MONITOR) {
+		mt792x_mutex_acquire(dev);
+		mt7925_mcu_set_sniffer(dev, vif, true);
+		mt7925_mcu_config_sniffer(mvif, ctx);
+		mt792x_mutex_release(dev);
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
